   <!--
   =====================================================================
   FLORIDA (FL) - NO STATE INCOME TAX TEST CASE
   =====================================================================

   Florida has NO state income tax on any type of income:
   - Pension income: NOT TAXED
   - Social Security benefits: NOT TAXED
   - Investment income (dividends/interest): NOT TAXED
   - All other income types: NOT TAXED

   Florida is one of 9 states with no personal income tax.
   This makes Florida particularly attractive to retirees.

   This test case validates:
   - Pension income ($45,000) is NOT taxed
   - Social Security benefits ($30,000) are NOT taxed (also not federally taxed)
   - Dividend income ($15,000) is NOT taxed
   - Interest income ($5,000) is NOT taxed
   - State tax = $0 for all retirement income

   Income breakdown:
   - Pension income: $45,000
   - Social Security: $30,000 (not taxable federally at this income level)
   - Qualified dividends: $15,000
   - Interest income: $5,000
   - Total for AGI: $65,000 (SS excluded)

   Expected Results:
   - Federal AGI: ~$65,000 (excludes non-taxable SS)
   - Federal Taxable: ~$50,000 (after standard deduction)
   - Federal Tax: ~$5,500 (approximate, with preferential dividend rate)
   - FL State Tax: $0 (no income tax)
   =====================================================================
   -->

